The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the API allows users to access resources based on user-supplied identifiers, such as `imageId`, without proper authorization checks. If the application does not verify whether the requesting user has permission to access the specified image, an attacker could manipulate the `imageId` parameter to access or share images that do not belong to them, leading to unauthorized data exposure. This lack of access control can compromise the privacy and security of user-uploaded images.

